WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.934 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-How are you, buddy?

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, man. I'm good.
How are you?

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm very good.

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do miss having you
here in person

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:09.075
because you often show up
in sartorial splendor.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you dress up at all
for us today?

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:14.381 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Eh, no, not really.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:17.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just sort of a green shirt
today.

00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:19.619 size:84% position:42%
You know what I thought
you were going to say

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:22.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
is I thought you were going to
say you missed my hugs.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
I do miss your hugs.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
But mostly while
I'm hugging you,

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.095 line:92%
I just want to have your style

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
What a very well-appointed
office, though.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.401 size:88% position:44%
Is it safe to say you're
in an office right now?

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:37.037 line:92%
-I'm actually not in an office

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.072 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Are you in a closet?

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:42.375 line:92%
-Yeah, this is -- [ Laughs ]

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.044 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I'm not that opulent.

00:00:44.044 --> 00:00:44.878 line:92%
No. It's like a little --

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:49.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like a TV room, basically
like a media room.

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:51.551 line:92%
-I want to ask this question

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:52.652 line:92%
You obviously -- None of us --

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not dressed up, either
for this

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.455 line:92%
because we're living in a time

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
where a lot of the standards
are lower.

00:00:57.457 --> 00:01:01.127
I know you just celebrated
an 11th wedding anniversary.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is a celebration like that
during a pandemic,

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
does it take the pressure of
a little bit?

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:09.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you cannot, obviously,
roll out the red carpet.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:10.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Yeah, totally.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, it's an opportunity
to kind of be like,

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.308
"Well, I guess I can't --
I guess I can't really --

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can't really
do anything for this."

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:23.083
You know, it's sad to thin
of that as an opportunity.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:25.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, but we did.
We kept it very simple.

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.020
I mean, I think last time
I was on there, actually,

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
we talked about my wife and I'
10th-anniversary trip.

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:36.129
-Yeah, which was a bit of a --
I guess a boating mishap, right?

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:36.763 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Like, you were outdoors.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were doing all the thing
we used to do.

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:42.102
And let's be honest, this year
went probably better for you

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:42.702 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh, yeah.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:45.171 size:75% position:38%
Well, anything where
I'm not throwing up

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.874 line:92%
off the back of a boat is --

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.776 size:81% position:41% line:92%
is much better for me.

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are --
You're in California right now

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:56.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is, based on everythin
you see and hear,

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very hot place to be
right now,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:01.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe a little bit of a scar
place to be right now.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you?
I know your kids are 8 and 6

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.225 line:92%
How are they handling school

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you guys
getting through it?

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.629 size:84% position:42%
Uh, I mean, everybody's
taking it in stride.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, look, I can't complain
I'm financially stable.

00:02:12.966 --> 00:02:16.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there's people in far worse
situations than I'm in.

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:19.205
You're right, though, California
does seem to be on fire.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't seem to stop my eyes
from watering.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm assuming that's
because of the fires.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:27.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
Either that or it's
I'm crying about something

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I'm, you know,
subconsciously unaware of.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:33.720
-Like a super-repressed thin
is coming out during this time

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's possible.
It's possible.

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:39.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I mean, we're teaching
our kids at home,

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.227
kind of splitting our days
between teaching the kids

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.397
and, you know,
trying to get our own work done.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:49.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, just kind o
riding this thing out.

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:49.736 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's not so bad.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:51.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, luckily,
I actually like my wife.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:54.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
We enjoy each other's company.
So, um, it's --

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:56.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's good.
I'm finding the same.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:58.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a very nice thing
to realize, like,

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.613 size:78% position:39%
"Oh, we're doing good
with all this time,"

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:03.082 line:92%
which is very nice to find out

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:06.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you --
How are 8 and 6 insofar

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:11.191
as they can handle attention
spans of doing school right now?

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That has been a struggle,
for sure,

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:15.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, I mean,
especially the kindergartner

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:20.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, he's very --
he's a very fidgety guy.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's active.
He's very social.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.237
He wants to be, you know,
moving around and stuff.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:27.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Zoom's not really conduciv
to that.

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.475 line:92%
And, you know, my kids are -

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.710 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I mean, they do okay,

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they're also a little bi
the kind of kids

00:03:32.745 --> 00:03:34.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
that would, like,
sit in the back of the class

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:35.915 line:92%
and, like, hope that the teacher

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
doesn't ever call on them
or notice them,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:42.088
which is a lot easier
to pull off when you're on Zoom.

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:44.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
As a matter of fact, actually,
the other day,

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.293 line:92%
I looked in the playroom,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:51.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is where my kindergartne
is doing Zooms.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.766
And the Zoom call was happening,
and I could hear it.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.736 size:81% position:41%
And I looked in there,
and he was just, like,

00:03:56.736 --> 00:04:01.708
draped across the chair,
like, in a Superman pose.

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:04.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, not paying attention
to the Zoom at all.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just, like, doing --
I don't know what he was doing

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was not doing school.
-It's good.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:13.019
It's good to give kids roo
to make their own choices.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.254 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:15.088 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-This is very exciting.

00:04:15.088 --> 00:04:19.659
You know, I think both you and I
are excited and delighted

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:22.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there even is a Season
of "A.P. Bio."

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
For those who don't know,
it was an NBC show

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:28.801
that then got picked up on NBC's
new streaming service, Peacock

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:34.307
And you guys had shot 8 episodes
of 10 when this hit.

00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.576 line:92%
Do you remember that day, like

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the decisions
were being made?

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause they were being mad
pretty quickly.

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember there was a lo
of talk about it.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:43.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember we were
a little stressed

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:45.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
about being able
to finish eight.

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:48.288
'Cause I remember thinking
if we can get eight out,

00:04:48.288 --> 00:04:50.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you can release
eight episodes.

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:53.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it almost feels like
a full season of television.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:56.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, so luckily,
we were able to get that done.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.865
I was also in the middle of,
I think, editing the episode

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:03.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I had directed
a couple weeks prior.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:04.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was in the middle
of editing that.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:07.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, you know,
things shut down.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.475 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, there was a par
of me that at the time

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:12.612
I was like, "Oh, well, this will
be a good opportunity

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:15.715 size:75% position:38%
to just, like, rest,
'cause I'm tired."

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, but luckily,
we got eight good episodes out

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:22.622 line:92%
-It's a delight to watch.

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:25.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the most jarring things
about watching it right no

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:27.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that it takes place
in a high school.

00:05:27.894 --> 00:05:32.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm wondering
if that is refreshing

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.132 line:92%
for people to look at a school

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:37.403
where no one is worried abou
things like social distancin

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.339 line:92%
or if it is like a horror movi

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:42.475 size:75% position:38%
to just watch people
touching each other

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
and bumping into each othe
in the hallways.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.714
I personally find it the former,
obviously.

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:51.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, yeah, it's strange
because you see that

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:53.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it seems like
such strange behavior now

00:05:53.586 --> 00:05:56.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see, like,
people talking face-to-fac

00:05:56.356 --> 00:05:57.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
hugging each other

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, being
in proximity with each other

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:00.993 size:81% position:41% line:92%
without wearing masks.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:02.528 line:92%
So it's both, like, horrifying

00:06:02.528 --> 00:06:04.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also like you pine for i
at the same time.

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:07.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know that there's
too many things you can watc

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you're both
horrified by it

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:12.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you pine for it
at the same time.

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:14.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have this incredible
supporting cast

00:06:14.974 --> 00:06:17.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Patton Oswalt,
obviously Paula Pell.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:20.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the things that's
really fun about this season

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:22.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you spend more time
in the classroom.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:24.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is one -- You know,
it's one those shows where -

00:06:24.984 --> 00:06:28.087
It's three seasons, but it's
the same kids in the classroom

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:30.723
And there's a really nice
chemistry with you guys.

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:32.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
It must be fun to, you know,
not only get to know

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:35.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
the characters better
and know how to react to them,

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:38.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
but to get to know
the actual actors, as well

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:41.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, God.
I adore this cast.

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm the luckiest man
in the world.

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.904 size:75% position:38%
Like, I love working
with these people.

00:06:44.904 --> 00:06:46.239 line:92%
I get to laugh all day long.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, every single --
all the students,

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:50.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
all the other teachers,
everybody is a --

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.311 line:92%
you know, a scene stealer.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:53.913 line:92%
And I mean that in a good way.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:56.315 line:92%
Like, they're all so funny

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:59.218 line:92%
And it just -- it tickles me

00:06:59.218 --> 00:07:01.921 line:92%
I'm having a blast, you know

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:02.588 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And the kids especially,

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they were, you know,
younger actors,

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:06.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's been really fun
to watch them

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
get more and more confiden
as, you know --

00:07:08.828 --> 00:07:12.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
In the third season, they came
in so sure of themselves.

00:07:12.832 --> 00:07:13.433 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And, you know,

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:15.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
that just makes them
more comfortable and funnier

00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:16.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
you can kind of riff

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:18.271 line:92%
and improv with them and stuff

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:19.505 line:92%
They've just been amazing.

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You are one of our
most excellent thespians

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:25.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it comes to playing
likeable jerks.

00:07:25.678 --> 00:07:27.947 line:92%
And I mean that sincerely.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:28.781 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Jack on this show is.

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know, over the course
of the series

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:31.684 line:92%
and certainly more this year

00:07:31.684 --> 00:07:34.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, he seems to like
where he is more

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
and like the people
he's around more.

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:37.356 line:92%
Is that more fun to play?

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:41.494
Or do you enjoy the more
irascible where he started

00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:44.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it's been more fu
for me

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:47.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it allows me
to play notes

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:50.236
that I haven't been able to play
as an actor very much.

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:52.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I mean,
my other character

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "It's Always Sunny
in Philadelphia"

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:58.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
is in no way, shape,
or form warm.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:07:59.545 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:01.047 line:92%
-To get to play that is nice

00:08:01.047 --> 00:08:03.716
And it's also nice because
it creates a lot of conflict

00:08:03.716 --> 00:08:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the character because,
you know,

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:07.119
my character still really
wants to think of himself

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:09.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
as this elitist
Hollywood philosopher.

00:08:09.856 --> 00:08:13.526
You know, but he's slowly
being faced with the fact

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:14.627 line:92%
that maybe he could be happy

00:08:14.627 --> 00:08:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
with just being
a hometown Toledo boy,

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:17.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is also
his worst nightmare.

00:08:17.864 --> 00:08:21.868
So there's this great tension,
you know, within the character

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:22.902 line:92%
that he wants to be one thin

00:08:22.902 --> 00:08:26.539
but he feels something else an
he can't quite give into it.

00:08:26.539 --> 00:08:29.041 line:92%
But he's definitely, like --

